<title>NEW ZEALAND: Foreign share of NZ govt securities falls in Sept.</title>
<headline>Foreign share of NZ govt securities falls in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The proportion of New Zealand government securities held by foreigners fell in September to 52.5 percent, compared to 54.5 percent in August, the Reserve Bank said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>			  Sept 1996	Aug 1996	   Sept 1995</p>
<p>			Value  Pct*     Value   Pct*     Value    Pct*</p>
<p>T Bills	   2,380.5  31.5    2,780.7  41.3    3,221.7   48.8</p>
<p>Govt Bonds     12,252.5  60.3   11,992.3  58.8    6,682.2   33.7</p>
<p>Total Govt Secs14,633.0  52.5   14,773.0  54.5    9,903.9   37.5</p>
<p>Benchmark Bonds 10/96		48.7    16.1	 48.7  16.1	 38.9   12.8</p>
<p>11/96	   1,055.8    51.6    1,070.7  48.5	775.4   31.6</p>
<p>07/97	     836.1    42.6    1,066.5  54.3	280.2   14.3</p>
<p>07/98	   2,018.7    82.4    1,883.5  76.9	489.6   20.0</p>
<p>02/00	   1,486.5    49.4    1,530.3  50.8	697.7   23.2</p>
<p>02/01	   1,147.0    63.7    1,119.8  65.9	 32.0    8.0</p>
<p>03/02	   1,550.0    61.7    1,531.6  61.0	749.1   29.8</p>
<p>04/04	   2,007.8    66.0    1,861.3  61.1    1,818.6   59.7</p>
<p>11/06	   2,005.4    72.2    1,803.4  64.9	810.7   45.6</p>
<p>02/16		96.5    29.3	 76.5  23.3	  0.0	-</p>
<p>* Represents non-residential holdings as a percentage of total securities in the hands market excluding RBNZ/Treasury holdings.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734746</p>
</text>
